@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+---
+id: task-002-fix-coupon-stacking-on-volume-discounts-inclusive-coupon-expiry-and-single-use-coupon-give-back-on-cancel
+type: task
+title: "Fix coupon stacking on volume discounts, inclusive coupon expiry, and single-use coupon give-back on cancel"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Reports handled
+
+1. Finance: an order combining a volume discount with a percentage coupon gets more off than it
+   should. Twelve notebooks at €5.00 each with a 10% coupon come to €48.00 of goods; expected €48.60.
+2. Luca (customer): the code AUTUMN was advertised as valid until 30 November. He ordered on
+   30 November and the code was refused as expired.
+3. Anna (customer): her receipt shows VAT on the delivery cost, €1.08 on €4.90 of shipping. She asks
+   that VAT stop being added to shipping, since delivery is a service, not goods.
+
+## Root causes and fixes
+
+1. `priceOrder` (`src/pricing.ts`) computed the percentage coupon's amount on the order's gross total
+   (`couponDiscount(coupon, grossTotal)`), instead of on the subtotal after the volume discount, as the
+   README requires ("a coupon ... applies to the order's subtotal after volume discounts"). This let a
+   percentage coupon take its percentage off the pre-volume-discount amount, stacking the two discounts
+   additively instead of compounding them on the already-discounted subtotal: 12 units at €5.00 (€60.00
+   gross) with a 10% volume discount and a 10% coupon gave €60 - €6 - €6 = €48.00, instead of
+   €60 - €6 - 10%-of-€54 = €48.60. Fixed by computing the coupon's base as `grossTotal - volumeTotal`
+   (the subtotal after volume discounts) before applying the coupon's percentage or fixed value, as
+   already implemented in `couponDiscount`/`capped`. The order-wide 50%-of-gross cap (`capped`) is
+   unaffected: it already bounded any fixed coupon's effect by room against gross, independent of this
+   base.
+2. `Coupons#redeemable` (`src/coupons.ts`) rejected a coupon as expired when `date` was on or after
+   `validUntil` (`compareDates(date, coupon.validUntil) >= 0`), excluding the last valid day entirely,
+   though the README states a coupon "is valid from its first day to its last day, both included."
+   Changed the comparison to `> 0`, so the coupon is only rejected on days strictly after `validUntil`.
+3. While verifying coupon behaviour end to end (place, quote, cancel), found that `OrderService#cancel`
+   (`src/orders.ts`) called `this.#coupons.giveBack(order.coupon, order.customer)`, passing the
+   customer's name where `Coupons#giveBack` expects the order id that `use()` recorded. Since a
+   customer name never matches an order id, a single-use coupon was never actually given back on
+   cancellation, contradicting the README ("Cancelling it returns its units and gives back its coupon,
+   if the coupon was single-use."). Not one of the three reports, but found directly while fixing the
+   other coupon issues and in clear contradiction of a documented rule, so fixed alongside them: changed
+   the call to pass `order.id`.
+
+   Anna's report (VAT on shipping) was investigated and is **not a code bug**: the README explicitly
+   states "Shipping is subject to VAT at the standard rate (22%), shown on its own line of the
+   receipt," and the code computes exactly that (€4.90 × 22% = €1.078, rounded half up to €1.08, the
+   figure on her receipt). Changing this would be a business-rule change, not a bug fix, and would
+   require updating the README's VAT section and sign-off from whoever owns that rule; see the
+   decision-log for this finding. No code or test changed for this report.
+
+## Tests
+
+Added one characterization test per fixed bug (red before the fix, green after), following the
+red/green testing directive, in `test/coupons.test.ts`:
+
+- "applies a percentage coupon to the subtotal after the volume discount, not the gross amount": 12
+  units of a €20.00 product with a 10% coupon, mirroring finance's ratios (volume discount €24.00,
+  coupon €21.60, goods €194.40 on a €240.00 gross order — the same 90% × 90% stacking finance expects).
+- "accepts a coupon on its last valid day": places an order on the coupon's `validUntil` day.
+- "gives a single-use coupon back when the order that used it is cancelled": cancels an order that used
+  a single-use coupon, then re-uses the coupon on a new order.
+
+`npm test` passes: 20/20 (17 before this task, 3 added).
+
+## Consequences
+
+No public API changed. Behaviour changes: a percentage or fixed coupon combined with a volume discount
+now takes less off than before (correctly, per the README) on orders that trigger both; a coupon is now
+accepted on its last valid day; cancelling an order now actually returns its single-use coupon. No
+migration needed: these bring the code in line with the already-documented business rules in
+`README.md`. Anna's VAT-on-shipping report did not lead to a code change; see the accompanying
+decision-log.
